PDFE GitHub #465: fix the push-button background fill in draw_push_button.

Upstream MuPDF 1.26.10 passes four arguments to a two-conversion
fz_append_printf format for the push-button background fill:
    fz_append_printf(ctx, buf, "0 0 %g %g re\nf\n", 0, 0, w, h);
so the two %g consume the leading 0, 0 and the width/height are dropped --
the fill becomes a degenerate 0 0 0 0 re and the button interior is never
painted. draw_check_button and the Tx/Ch fills in the same file use the
correct two-argument form. Drop the two spurious leading zeros so the push
button fills its box like every other widget.

--- a/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c
+++ b/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c
@@ -3070,7 +3070,7 @@
 		if (has_bg)
 		{
 			fz_append_printf(ctx, buf, "%g %g %g rg\n", bg[0], bg[1], bg[2]);
-			fz_append_printf(ctx, buf, "0 0 %g %g re\nf\n", 0, 0, w, h);
+			fz_append_printf(ctx, buf, "0 0 %g %g re\nf\n", w, h);
 		}
 		if (has_bc && b > 0)
 		{
